    <string-array name="first_aid_summaries">
        <item>Control external bleeding</item>
        <item>First aid for thermal burns</item>
        <item>Immobilize the injured limb</item>
        <item>Heimlich maneuver</item>
        <item>Adult CPR</item>
        <item>First aid for loss of consciousness</item>
        <item>Managing poisoning</item>
        <item>Rapid cooling</item>
        <item>Protect the person during a seizure</item>
        <item>Clean and dress wounds</item>
    </string-array>

    <string-array name="first_aid_details">
        <item>Apply direct pressure to the wound with a clean cloth, raise the injured limb when appropriate, do not remove an embedded object, keep firm pressure until bleeding stops, and call emergency services immediately if bleeding is severe.</item>
        <item>Cool the burn under cool running water for 15-20 minutes. Do not use ice, toothpaste, or butter. Cover with a sterile non-stick dressing and do not burst blisters.</item>
        <item>Do not move the injured person unless necessary. Immobilize the injured limb with a temporary splint, apply a cold compress to reduce swelling, and call emergency services.</item>
        <item>Stand behind the person, place your fist above the navel, grasp it with the other hand, and give 5 firm inward-and-upward thrusts. Repeat until the obstruction is expelled.</item>
        <item>Check responsiveness and breathing, call emergency services, begin 30 chest compressions at 100-120 per minute, then give 2 rescue breaths if trained, and continue until help arrives.</item>
        <item>Lay the person on their back, raise the legs about 30 cm, loosen tight clothing, do not give anything by mouth, and seek emergency help if unconsciousness continues.</item>
        <item>Do not induce vomiting unless directed by a poison center. Call emergency services immediately, keep the product container, and monitor breathing.</item>
        <item>Move the person to a cool place, remove excess clothing, cool the body with wet towels, give fluids only if fully conscious, and call emergency services immediately.</item>
        <item>Move the person away from furniture, place something soft under the head, do not put anything in the mouth, and after the seizure ends place the person on their side.</item>
        <item>Wash the wound with clean water, disinfect it, cover it with a sterile dressing, and watch for signs of infection.</item>
    </string-array>

